WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.701
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.604
You're here.
You're watching. Thank you.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.305
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:08.707
Let's get to some news, guys.

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:12.879
This week, in a company memo,
the CEO of Delta Airlines

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:16.749
refused to use the term
Delta variant

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:21.221
and only referred to the virus
by its scientific name.

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:23.189
I guess that explains why pilots
have been saying,

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:26.593
"Welcome aboard. Thank you
for flying B.1.617.2 Airlines."

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:27.993
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.993 --> 00:00:30.663
Apparently, he's afraid that
if he says Delta too many times,

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.499
the virus will show up
like Candyman.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.568
Yeah, he's doing anything he can

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.904
to distance Delta
from the variant.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.305
Today, he said, "From now on,

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.207
our airline's pronounced
Del-tay."

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.109
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.444
That's right. Delta is in
a pretty weird situation,

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:47.480
but this is nice --
Another company just released

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.616
a message of support.
Watch this.

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:52.652
-We sympathize with
Delta CEO Ed Bastian.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.920
Hang in there.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.023
The only piece of advice
we could offer is to be patient.

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:59.859
And before long, your company
name won't be associated

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.927
with something so horrific.

00:01:01.927 --> 00:01:05.164
-A message from Ebola Farms
Baked Goods and Treats.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:07.000 line:0%
Put a little Ebola in your day.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.635
-Yeah.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.103
Ebola Farms.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.738
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:14.173
What?

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:15.374
I love that bread.

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:18.644
-I love Ebola Farms.
-Yeah, that's the best.

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:20.813
And they make bread.
-Yeah. I didn't know that.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:21.881
I just thought it was a farm.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.083
-Yeah, you'd think
it'd be a bakery.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.885
You think it'd be Ebola Bakery
or something.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.987
-Got a bunch of pretzels,
anything you want.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.088
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.124
Oh, my God.
-Any type of carb?

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.259
-Any kind of carb,
any kind of baked bread.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.394
They got strudel.

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.896
Oh, delicious. Delicious.
-Oh, strudel.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.032
Guys, get this,
a new report found

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.468
that nearly all
U.S. government agencies

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:44.403
are using facial
recognition technology.

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:46.539
[ Audience groaning ]

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:47.673
Americans are like, "Whoa,

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:49.208
I don't want something
scanning my face,"

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.943
and then went back
to pulling down their masks

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:52.211
to unlock their phones.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:53.879
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:55.581
Yep, most U.S.
government agencies

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:58.817
are now using some form of
facial recognition technology.

00:01:58.817 --> 00:02:00.653
But unfortunately,
it's having a little trouble

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:03.089
correctly identifying
people's faces,

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.991
and some can't even recognize
members of Congress.

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:07.193
I'll show you what I mean.

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.762
For example, it thought
Congressman Austin Scott

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.331
was the 40-year-old virgin.

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:12.364
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:13.800
See what I mean?
-Wow.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.902
-They're not recognizing --
-Yeah, it's not working right.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.569
-No, it's not working correctly.
Next up,

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:20.539
it thought Congressman
Dean Phillips was Doug Funnie.

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:22.241
-Really?

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.409
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.911
That's not even a real person.

00:02:25.911 --> 00:02:27.413
-What?
-That's a cartoon.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.647
-I know it's a cartoon.

00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:30.616
-Wow. This is not
working well at all.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.418
-Can we see that again
just to make sure?

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.153
That's --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:35.888
It's not working.
-Wow, it's not working.

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:37.891
You're right.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:40.193
-Next, it thought
Congressman Sam Graves

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:42.161
was that carnival game
with the clown face.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.262
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:45.531
-I mean, it's just
totally not working.

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:47.366
-That's not good at all.
-No, it's not good.

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:51.437
